From 0e96ca1c0a0b888836d7e09ac3cca1f8425722d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:27:01 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat(edm): Wire Contour skim passes - per-pass condition,
 offset and direction

A rough pass then N skims, each naming its own machine condition (its
offset is that condition's wire radius + gap) and optionally walked
the other way round. Skims ride the op params (file / MCP JSON
`skims`, absent when empty), EditOperationParams and the stamp. The
command door refuses a skim naming no condition or an unstated one, a
pass nearer the profile than the finishing pass, a skim farther out
than the pass before it, and a skim condition for another wire - each
by name. The generator runs the single-pass generator per pass at its
own offset; the wire stream announces each skim with a mid-section
PARAM EdmCondition and wire-iso.cps selects it (comp off again) with
the wire still threaded. Rough-only output is byte-identical to #533's
golden; new golden wire_contour_punch_skims.nc.

Fixes #538

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
